      "message": "I am not sure this toggle is enough to allow WaitAny on any thread.\n\n- Front-end\u0027s WaitAny will call [WaitQueueSerials here](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/src/dawn/native/EventManager.cpp;drc\u003d0bd06bf896dd685d16fa790986344929e12ed5a6;l\u003d197)\n- Which in turn will call [Queue::WaitForQueueSerial](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/src/dawn/native/EventManager.cpp;drc\u003d0bd06bf896dd685d16fa790986344929e12ed5a6;l\u003d164)\n- Then triggers [Queue::WaitForQueueSerialImpl](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/src/dawn/native/ExecutionQueue.cpp;drc\u003d0bd06bf896dd685d16fa790986344929e12ed5a6;l\u003d91)\n- The OpenGL\u0027s implementation will call [eglClientWaitSync](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/src/dawn/native/opengl/QueueGL.cpp;drc\u003d0bd06bf896dd685d16fa790986344929e12ed5a6;l\u003d200) which requires a current context. I don\u0027t think it will work without `GLAllowContextOnMultiThreads` toggle.",
